## 4. The Affective Drift Proof (Step 4)

We mathematically proved the existence of **Affective Drift** ($P = E \neq I$). 

When a viewer is in a Happy state (Q1) and watches another Happy clip (Maintenance), their self-reported valence shift is stable. However, when they "Switch" into Q1 from a different emotion, their body (I2) lags behind their mind (I1), creating the "Drift" effect.

![Maintenance vs Drift Proof](file:///d:/BTP/btp2/salmamaterials/_plots/_maintenance_vs_drift_proof.png)
_The clinical proof: The Maintenance group shows a much narrower, stable valence shift compared to the Drift/Switching group._

