## 5. Statistical Significance Table

We conducted independent t-tests on the distributions.

| Hypothesis | τ | t-stat | p-value | Significant? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Hyp-1** (Agreement) | 0.50 | -3.40 | 0.0006 | **Yes** |
| **Hyp-7** (Body-Clip Align) | 0.50 | 9.69 | < 0.0001 | **Yes** |
| **Hyp-1** (Agreement) | 0.75 | -3.84 | 0.0001 | **Yes** |
| **Hyp-7** (Body-Clip Align) | 1.00 | 4.50 | < 0.0001 | **Yes** |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hyp-7** is consistently the most significant result across all thresholds, proving that physiological signals (Fitbit) are much more consistent with the expressed content of the clip than self-reported surveys are during transitions.

